1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,500
Every AI reply sounds the same.
Polite, tidy, and nothing like you.

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:09,500
My friends would spot it in a second.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,500
This is SaySo, a keyboard
that writes the way you'd say it.

4
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:18,500
I type a plain draft…
tap the sparkle…

5
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:23,500
and get three versions in my own voice.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,000
And I don't send one long paragraph,
I send bursts.

7
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:34,500
So SaySo does too: a series,
stacked like notifications.

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Tap, send. Next. Send.

9
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:44,500
Same meaning, my rhythm.

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,000
A friend asks for help on Saturday,
and I can't.

11
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:52,500
I double-tap the back of my phone.

12
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:56,500
SaySo grabs the screen
and asks who it's for.

13
00:00:56,600 --> 00:01:01,000
I add a note:
politely decline, I'm busy.

14
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:07,000
Muse Spark reads the chat,
my own model writes the replies.

15
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:11,000
Pick one, paste, send.

16
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:14,500
I never left Telegram.

17
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Where does my voice come from?
My own chats.

18
00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:23,000
I export one from WhatsApp
and drop it in.

19
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:28,000
SaySo asks which one is me:
it only learns from my side.

20
00:01:28,100 --> 00:01:33,000
It reads how I react, builds my profile,

21
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:37,500
then tests itself on messages
it hasn't seen.

22
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:44,500
Sounds like me: 78%.
Generic AI: 41%.

23
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,500
And it keeps learning.

24
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:52,500
Too long? Thumbs down: "shorter."

25
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:57,500
It rewrites, and remembers the rule
for next time.

26
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:04,500
Every message I send with SaySo's keyboard
becomes a new example right away.

27
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:09,500
And I can delete any of them.

28
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Under the hood: Meta's Muse Spark 1.3
reads the chat and drafts.

29
00:02:15,100 --> 00:02:20,000
My own LoRA on Muse Glimmer 30B
puts it in my words,

30
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:23,500
guided by my style profile
and real examples.

31
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:29,500
Form similarity goes from 0.67 to 0.94;
chrF from 41 to 51.

32
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:33,500
Only my own messages are stored.

33
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:39,500
Other people's messages and screenshots
are read in memory, then dropped.

34
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:44,500
SaySo.
Your words, your voice.

35
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:49,500
And you always press send.
